### Description
This Terraform program creates an AWS S3 bucket to store images that will be displayed on a website. It ensures that the bucket is publicly accessible, allowing images to be viewed directly from the internet.

### Terraform HCL Program
```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

variable "bucket_name_prefix" {
  default = "my-website-images-bucket"
}

resource "random_string" "random_suffix" {
  length = 8
  special = false
  upper = false
  lower = false
  number = true
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket" "website_images_bucket" {
  bucket = "${var.bucket_name_prefix}-${random_string.random_suffix.result}"
  acl    = "public-read"
  tags = {
    Name        = "Website Images Bucket"
    Environment = "Development"
  }
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket_policy" "website_images_bucket_policy" {
  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.website_images_bucket.id

  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Effect   = "Allow"
        Principal = "*"
        Action   = [
          "s3:GetObject"
        ]
        Resource = [
          "${aws_s3_bucket.website_images_bucket.arn}/*"
        ]
      }
    ]
  })
}
```

### Explanation
- **Provider Configuration**: The `aws` provider is configured with the `region` set to `us-east-1`.
- **Variables**: A variable `bucket_name_prefix` is defined with a default value of `my-website-images-bucket`. This allows for easy customization of the bucket name.
- **Random String**: A `random_string` resource is used to generate a random suffix for the bucket name, ensuring uniqueness.
- **S3 Bucket**: An `aws_s3_bucket` resource is created with the generated bucket name. The bucket is set to have a public-read ACL, allowing anyone to access the objects within the bucket.
- **Bucket Policy**: An `aws_s3_bucket_policy` resource is attached to the bucket to allow public access to all objects. The policy grants the `GetObject` action to all principals (`*`).

